course: dictionary
lesson: 869
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and bill is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it: they are its context. «Fixed costs are bills that come every month, like rent, energy and council tax» tells you that a bill here is something you have to pay.
explain: Now read «A bill goes through readings (debates), a committee that checks it line by line, and amendments (changes)... before it becomes law.» Here a bill is a plan for a new law, not money. The clues are readings, committee and law. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then put your meaning in place of the word and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Bill can also be a bird's beak. In «duck-billed dinosaurs», the bill is the beak, which is why the name is about a duck. Bill can even be a boy's name. In «she puts Bill the Lizard in upside down», the capital letters and the word Lizard show that Bill is a name.
fact: Bill can mean a piece of paper money. In the UK it is called a note.
fact: Bill can mean a paper that shows how much you must pay, as in «pay the bill» or «electric bill».
fact: A bird's beak is also called a bill, and different birds have bills of different shapes for different food.
fact: Bill can mean a plan for a new law, and it is debated before it becomes law.
fact: Bill is also a boy's name.
exercise: «Fixed costs are bills that come every month, like rent, energy and council tax.» What does bill mean here? | A plan for a new law | A bird's beak | * A paper showing how much you must pay | A boy called Bill
exercise: «A bill goes through readings (debates), a committee... before it becomes law.» In this sentence, what is a bill? | A name | A bird's beak | * A plan for a new law | Paper money
exercise: «Others had no armour at all: duck-billed dinosaurs ground plants with hundreds of packed teeth.» What is a bill in this sentence? | * A beak | A law | A dollar note | A list of costs
test: Maya says, «She paid the bill at the restaurant.» What does bill mean? | * A paper showing how much you must pay | A bird's beak | A plan for a new law | A bank note from the UK
test: In «she puts Bill the Lizard in upside down», what is Bill? | * The name of a lizard | A paper showing what to pay | Paper money | A bird's beak
exam: «Let's split the bill» means | Share a paper note | Divide the bird food | * Share the cost of the meal | Make a new law
